WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.091 --> 00:00:01.171
(surf music)

00:00:01.171 --> 00:00:04.367
- [Lambert] There's so many
reasons why I do what I do.

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:07.670
I love surfing and I love helping people.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.271
I think if everybody
found what they love to do

00:00:10.271 --> 00:00:11.989
and what they were designed to do,

00:00:11.989 --> 00:00:14.140
and used that gift to help others,

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.057
this world would look so different.

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:22.995
(bright music)

00:00:22.995 --> 00:00:24.339
My name's Lambert Lo.

00:00:24.339 --> 00:00:26.899
And I'm a surf instructor.

00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:29.402
I was living in Hawaii, living the dream,

00:00:29.402 --> 00:00:33.042
teaching surfing to
billionaires and celebrities.

00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:35.036
And at the end of the day,
something was missing.

00:00:35.036 --> 00:00:37.463
And I knew in my heart that
I needed to come back

00:00:37.463 --> 00:00:40.231
to where it all started.

00:00:40.231 --> 00:00:42.095
I grew up in California,

00:00:42.095 --> 00:00:45.447
and the ocean was where I
felt the most connected.

00:00:45.447 --> 00:00:47.639
I came back and started a non-profit

00:00:47.639 --> 00:00:49.556
called The Mix Academy.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.380
(lively music)

00:00:57.380 --> 00:00:59.318
One of the things that
come out of The Mix Academy

00:00:59.318 --> 00:01:00.886
is the surf school.

00:01:00.886 --> 00:01:03.374
And I brought that gift of surfing

00:01:03.374 --> 00:01:06.849
here with some of the people
that need the most smiles.

00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:08.159
Push up on the side.

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:08.992
Stand up, go.

00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:10.548
My current class consists

00:01:10.548 --> 00:01:13.619
of a refugee from North Korea,

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:16.503
Nathan, a nine-year-old
who's visually impaired,

00:01:16.503 --> 00:01:20.503
and Shannon, a veteran
going through alcoholism.

00:01:21.676 --> 00:01:22.717
The School of the Misfits is a place

00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:24.087
where you can belong.

00:01:24.087 --> 00:01:27.082
On land, everyone looks at
us a little differently,

00:01:27.082 --> 00:01:28.562
but when you're in the water,

00:01:28.562 --> 00:01:30.729
the water washes all that off.

00:01:32.795 --> 00:01:33.628
Woo!

00:01:35.386 --> 00:01:39.210
Surfing, like life, is
full of ups and downs.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.028
There's waves that are coming

00:01:41.028 --> 00:01:43.556
and you can't stop that from coming.

00:01:43.556 --> 00:01:44.701
The pain's gonna come.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:45.992
What you can control is yourself

00:01:45.992 --> 00:01:48.160
and how you're gonna react.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.128
You can choose to paddle for it,

00:01:50.128 --> 00:01:51.848
embrace it and adapt to it,

00:01:51.848 --> 00:01:53.263
and enjoy the ride,

00:01:53.263 --> 00:01:56.627
or this wave's gonna come
and it's gonna knock you out

00:01:56.627 --> 00:01:58.167
and it's gonna wipe you out.

00:01:58.167 --> 00:01:59.865
Catching the wave is a great feeling,

00:01:59.865 --> 00:02:01.503
helping others catch their first wave

00:02:01.503 --> 00:02:03.775
is a greater feeling.

00:02:03.775 --> 00:02:06.260
To watch that smile just ear to ear,

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.427
and knowing that, man, that's
gonna change someone's life.

